PS3-G29-2  635741dd makes the CMake build impossible with the Ninja generator (dependency cycle)

635741dd (v7.0.18, "enable parallel build with older Bison versions") listed scotch.h and ptscotch.h among the
sources of the executables dummysizes and ptdummysizes, i.e. of the very programs that generate them, while the
custom commands producing scotch.h/ptscotch.h DEPEND on dummysizes. Unix Makefiles accepts the cycle, Ninja rejects it.

Usage:   ./run.sh <scotch source tree> [workdir]     (needs cmake, ninja, make; the source tree is not modified)

Observed (CMake 4.4.4, Ninja 1.x):
  v7.0.17                       Ninja: build OK       Unix Makefiles: build OK
  635741dd^ (parent commit)     Ninja: build OK       Unix Makefiles: build OK
  v7.0.18 (pristine)            Ninja: FAILED         Unix Makefiles: build OK
      ninja: error: dependency cycle: src/libscotch/dummysizes -> src/libscotch/CMakeFiles/dummysizes.dir/dummysizes.c.o
          -> cmake_object_order_depends_target_dummysizes -> src/include/scotch.h -> src/libscotch/dummysizes
  v7.0.18 + our 232-patch series            Ninja: FAILED (the series does not touch this)
  v7.0.18 + series + the fix commit         Ninja: build OK       Unix Makefiles: build OK
Fix: patch "Bugfix: do not make the header generators depend on the headers they generate".
